   "source": [
    "#fit the model on trained data\n",
    "lm_spend = LinearRegression()\n",
    "lm_spend.fit(X_train_spend, y_train)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 412,
   "id": "9f098f17-8b56-49cd-96e3-412a9d98b247",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#predict on training data\n",
    "y_pred_train_spend = lm_spend.predict(X_train_spend)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 413,
   "id": "47e62e72-5675-42c2-bdb6-2ea6231a0beb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#plot and add regression line\n",
    "plt.scatter(X_train_spend, y_train, color='red', alpha=0.6)\n",
    "plt.plot(X_train_spend, y_pred_train_spend, color='green', label='Regression Line')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Loyalty Points vs Spending Score (Training Set)\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Spending Score\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Loyalty Points\")\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 414,
   "id": "1030bfd2-abe7-47c8-8976-a2c231f2692e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Spending Score model parameters:\n",
      "const            -75.052663\n",
      "spending_score    33.061693\n",
      "dtype: float64\n",
      "\n",
      "Spending Score model standard errors:\n",
      "const             45.930554\n",
      "spending_score     0.814419\n",
      "dtype: float64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#parameters for spending score \n",
    "X_sm_spend = sm.add_constant(X_spend)\n",
    "model_spend = sm.OLS(y, X_sm_spend).fit()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Spending Score model parameters:\")\n",
    "print(model_spend.params)\n",
    "print(\"\\nSpending Score model standard errors:\")\n",
    "print(model_spend.bse)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3383ca6c-a99f-46f7-a975-16aba4b8832a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Based on the analysis of how spending score, remuneration and age influences loyalty points we can detect a strong and positive correlation for spending score and remuneration. There is instead a negative correlation regarding age and loyalty points. The coefficients of 34.19 and 33.06 for remuneration and spending score, rispectively, show that the more the customers spend and the more they are engaged, more they are rewarded with loyalty points. There is an oppostive relation regarding the age, a coefficient of -4.01 tell us that to an increase of one year age old corrispond a decrease of 4 points. A relatively low standard error suggest that the conclusion we deduced are reliable.\n",
    "\n",
    "From a business point of view, the insights I provide can could be used for marketing strategies. Low-spending customers could be targeted to incentivize low-spending attitude. Future analysis could include clustering customers into group to anlyse if their behavior have some substantial change, or to suit marketing proposals."
   ]
  },
