     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# import the module\n",
    "from sklearn import tree\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 10))\n",
    "tree.plot_tree(regressor, fontsize=10, filled=True, feature_names=x_train.columns, rounded=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2d1fda56-8336-4f03-8c64-f240b8549d97",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Train R² score: 1.0 This means the algorithm memorise the train set perfectly\n",
    "- Test R² score: 0.9960547369776616 the model is generalising well to unseen data in the selected split\n",
    "\n",
    "Conclusion. The train test could mean that the model won't generalise to other data in the future.\n",
    "So there is a high risk of multi-collinearity\n",
    "\n",
    "we will try in the following code to apply some pruning "
   ]
  },
