     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Train R² after pruning: 0.9157\n",
      "Test R² after pruning: 0.9073\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#calculate R² after the pruning\n",
    "train_score = regressor.score(x_train, y_train)\n",
    "test_score = regressor.score(x_test, y_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Train R² after pruning: {train_score:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'Test R² after pruning: {test_score:.4f}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "147a3555-891a-4cee-ab88-c000ec00d7e5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Conclusions after pruning:\n",
    "\n",
    "- the train R² of 0.91 explain 91% of the variance of training set\n",
    "- the test R² of 0.915 tells us that the model works well with unseen data\n",
    "\n",
    "the model is not overfitting anymore"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "304460bb-4cef-4c06-925d-9077733a8c3f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The decision tree we built have a strong fit of 91% and can classify new data 91% of the time. The tree identifies most impactful factors like remuneration and spending score. More insights could emerge from exploring multicollinearity.This model is useful as a guide to understand which customer are more likely to earn more loyalty points and create targeted marketing campaigns. This is useful in order to make customers more involved, increase the profit of the company and increment the return on investment of the marketing campaings and of  the company overall. \n",
    "Inform stakeholder decisions\n",
    "the decision tree we improve can be usefull to the stakeholder in numerous ways:\n",
    "\n",
    "- segment the customers more strategically\n",
    "- inform the marketing office regarding personalise promotions\n",
    "- adjust loyalty points on the basis of the characteristics that drive loyalty points\n",
    "- predict loyalty points for hypotetical customers\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "15aa2287-7576-450e-9a45-62e893e973f3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "3. making prediction with clustering.\n",
    "In the following promts I will use the k-measn clustering to identify th optimal number of clusters,\n",
    "in the 'remuneration' and 'spending_score' columns. I will later apply and plot the data using the created segment"
   ]
  },
