   ],
   "source": [
    "# Check the number of observations per predicted class.\n",
    "x_plot_4['K-Means Predicted'].value_counts()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cfd9f36c-eeb4-45cc-b930-5cab93fea08a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The best fitting number of cluster could be k=5.\n",
    "The silhoutte score ( 0.582) is the closer to 1, which tells us the clusters are better separated. \n",
    "The pairplot is not that useful because for all the four pairplots there is a one cluster which is bigger compare to the others.\n",
    "Even through the number of observations per prediced class the number of observations that looks like more balanced is k=5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 446,
   "id": "f28094c1-bf36-430b-8f80-18f523fbedde",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Silhouette Score for k=5: 0.582\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#final decision k=5\n",
    "#plot for k=5\n",
    "kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=5, \n",
    "                init='k-means++', \n",
    "                random_state=42)\n",
    "labels = kmeans.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "#add cluster labels to the dataframe\n",
    "df3['cluster'] = labels\n",
    "\n",
    "#compute the silhouette score\n",
    "sil_score = silhouette_score(X_scaled, labels)\n",
    "print(f\"Silhouette Score for k=5: {sil_score:.3f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "#plot the clustered data\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(data=df3, \n",
    "                x='remuneration', \n",
    "                y='spending_score', \n",
    "                hue='cluster', \n",
    "                palette='Set1')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.title('K-means Clustering with k=5')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Remuneration')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Spending Score')\n",
    "plt.legend(title='Cluster')\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
