    "from wordcloud import WordCloud\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "#combine all features into a single string\n",
    "text = ' '.join([' '.join(words) if isinstance(words, list) else str(words) \n",
    "                 for words in df4_copy['summary']])\n",
    "\n",
    "#generate word cloud\n",
    "wordcloud = WordCloud(width=800, height=400, background_color='white').generate(text)\n",
    "\n",
    "#plot the word cloud\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(15, 7.5))\n",
    "plt.imshow(wordcloud, interpolation='bilinear')\n",
    "plt.axis('off')\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d655742a-77ef-4517-9364-2d5a26f2c267",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The words clound is a useful and intuitive tool to idenfity the frequent words in a text.\n",
    "Words cloud can give us a general sense of the words that turn around the commments section of the Turtle Game's website.\n",
    "The most common words are: five, star, great, good, game, awesome, excellent, awesome, age, nice, family, quality useful gift.\n",
    "\n",
    "However It is not appropriate for analysisng the senitment of the comments and summary sections.\n",
    "A much better sense of the sentiment will come after we will add the frequency distribution and the polarity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "10c15593-e2ea-4024-90fd-691c33e97c4e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Determine the frequency distribution and polarity"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 463,
   "id": "28b5ad1b-f354-448c-85cf-eff0c0b31dd7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[('game', 1990), ('great', 875), ('fun', 770), ('one', 568), ('play', 528), ('like', 468), ('stars', 464), ('love', 416), ('good', 381), ('five', 362), ('really', 349), ('get', 333), ('tiles', 317), ('book', 316), ('time', 309)]\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
